{
 "node": "GeoProximitySensor",
 "mode": "scene",
 "note": "X_ITE 16.6.0 wraps a ProximitySensor. size 0 0 0 is never active, size -1 -1 -1 always, the box test is inclusive. position_changed, orientation_changed and centerOfRotation_changed are in the frame of the sensor's parent (the nested sensor, 10 m east and turned 90 degrees, reads the camera at (-12,0,-10)); geoCoord_changed is the same local position read through geoSystem and GeoOrigin (as in GeoTouchSensor: only the true position of the viewer when nothing moves the sensor). At the start the camera at (0,0,12) is 12 m south of the origin: latitude -1.085e-4. `geoCenter` is copied to `center` as raw numbers when it is written at run time and the attribute of a file is ignored (PG stays inactive, PC with center written is active). On leaving, the first position outside (60,0,0) is announced before isActive false. The fixture animates a small box with a TimeSensor: X_ITE draws on demand and only notices an enter after a pure camera move when something else keeps it drawing.",
 "gaps": [
  "a sensor inside a Transform reports geoCoord_changed of the local position (X_ITE's shortcut), not the viewer's geographic position",
  "X_ITE sends isActive false and exitTime twice when the sensor is disabled while active: the bridge sends them once (the fixture asserts at least one)",
  "the viewer's own navigation (mouse, keys) is not simulated: the camera is moved by writing the Viewpoint position",
  "events carry the pose of the camera in the same frame (no frame of lag as in X_ITE)"
 ],
